<text transformations="translations" pos="26.7852 295.96" stroke="black" type="minipage" width="527.902" height="18.866" depth="13.9" valign="top">From the proof, the edges from $x_1$ to $x_2$ must be consecutive or there are not even edges. And also their relative order is even in both rotations of $x_1$ and $x_2$. we can consider concatinating all the edges from $x_1$ to $x_2$, the graph has a x-monotone embedding</text>
